; What phase 1 decides today, written by EgglogExport next to the terms, and
; where egglog agrees with it.  Load after rules.egg.

; TodayUp v n d c: today's matcher reads site v as div(n, d, Up) under
; condition c (0 = always).  The facts file's ";@today v kind" line says which
; row matched (bias, indicator, guarded, masked).
(relation TodayUp (i64 Term Term i64))
; TodayExact v: division v is by the constant 1.
(relation TodayExact (i64))

; Agree v: egglog finds the same reading, with n and d equal up to the merge
; rules (so a product written in another order still agrees).
(relation Agree (i64))
(rule ((Intent v n d c) (TodayUp v n d c)) ((Agree v)) :ruleset match)
